From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:31:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: keep a system thread in its creator's pseudo-process

mmdevapi's driver starts an audio client's timer thread itself since
wine-11.18 (create_unix_thread, PsCreateSystemThread), and that thread
has no TEB. ios_jit_current_peb returned NULL for it, so the thread sent
its pipes on the root process's master socket, and the server killed it:

  [srv-own] receive_fd BAD tid=00c4 on pid=0020 ... cause=WRONG-PROCESS
  [srv-kill] kill_thread tid=00c4 pid=0028 violent=1

In a game's process no event-driven WASAPI client was ever signalled
again. Media Foundation's audio renderer is one: it took six samples,
its clock stayed at 0, and the media engine's video sink held after two
frames, so Monster Train's intro video (AVPro, IMFMediaEngine) never
played or ended, on either backend.

PsCreateSystemThread now records the creator's pseudo-process in the
thread's data (patches/wine-unix 0023), and ios_jit_current_peb returns
it for a thread without a TEB.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-09-monster-train-audio-timer.md
Offered-upstream: no; pseudo-processes exist only on the iOS port
---
 build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c  | 9 +++++++++
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c | 8 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c
index c9fbee2..b333906 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c
@@ -1738,6 +1738,15 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI PsCreateSystemThread( HANDLE *handle, ACCESS_MASK access, OBJECT
     if ((status = create_server_thread( handle, &data, access, attr, start, param, flags, TRUE )))
         return status;
 
+#ifdef WINE_IOS
+    {
+        /* Playport: the thread has no TEB, so ios_jit_current_peb finds its
+         * pseudo-process here; without it the thread spoke on the root's
+         * master socket and the server killed it (WRONG-PROCESS). */
+        extern void *ios_jit_current_peb(void);
+        data->ios_owner_peb = ios_jit_current_peb();
+    }
+#endif
     if ((status = spawn_thread( data )))
     {
         NtClose( *handle );
diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
index 5f4c488..9b6b55d 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
@@ -3990,7 +3990,13 @@ void *ios_jit_current_peb(void)
         cur_teb = *(char **)(tsd_base + ios_teb_tls_slot_offset);
     }
     if (!cur_teb && ios_teb_tls_key) cur_teb = pthread_getspecific(ios_teb_tls_key);
-    if (!cur_teb) return NULL;
+    if (!cur_teb)
+    {
+        /* A system thread (PsCreateSystemThread: mmdevapi's audio timer) has
+         * no TEB; it belongs to the pseudo-process that created it. */
+        struct thread_data *data = thread_data_key ? pthread_getspecific( thread_data_key ) : NULL;
+        return data && !data->teb ? data->ios_owner_peb : NULL;
+    }
     return ((TEB *)cur_teb)->Peb;
 }
 
-- 
